This reading is to document the process of launching the robot in the forest environment

Repository link: faiza-khatri/go2_ros2_sim_py

To get Gazebo running:
ros2 launch gazebo_sim launch_sim.launch.py
(Run generate_world.py when you first pull the repository)

To install fast-lio:
- Go to LivoxSDK2 folder inside main workspace src
- Run:
    mkdir build
    cd build
    cmake .. && make -j
    sudo make install

- Go to ws_livox/src/livox_driver_ros2
- Run:
    source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.sh
    ./build.sh jazzy

- Go to the main src of the workspace
- Run:
    rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -r -y
    colcon build --symlink-install
    source install/setup.bash

- Pray


To get Fast-Lio running:
- In workspace, go to FAST_LIO_ROS2/config/mid360.yaml
- Change map_file_path to wherever you want to save pcd files
- Run:
    ros2 launch fast_lio mapping.launch.py config_path:=/path/to/workspace/src/FAST_LIO_ROS2/config
- To save map:
    ros2 service call /map_save std_srvs/srv/Trigger {}



Set TROT mode:
ros2 topic pub --once /robot1/robot_mode quadropted_msgs/msg/RobotModeCommand "{mode: 'TROT', robot_id: 1}"
Teleop:
ros2 run teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard --ros-args -r /cmd_vel:=/robot1/cmd_vel

Getting 3D lidar data as a topic:
The Go2 robot has a gpu_lidar sensor defined in go2_description/xacro/gazebo.xacro.
- configured as a 16-channel LiDAR (VLP-16 equivalent) with a full 360 degree horizontal sweep, 
- 16 vertical channels spanning +-15 degrees (manually added)
- a maximum range of 12m. 
Data is outputted as gz.msgs.PointCloudPacked internally.

At this point, the sensor outputted two topics on the Gazebo transport layer:
  /robot1/points         - gz.msgs.LaserScan format
  /robot1/points/points  - gz.msgs.PointCloudPacked format

The packed point cloud on /robot1/points/points is the one bridged to ROS 2.

The bridge is configured by:
gazebo_multi_nav2_world.launch.py under the per-robot node definitions. The correct bridge argument for the LiDAR is:

  /{namespace}/points/points@sensor_msgs/msg/PointCloud2[gz.msgs.PointCloudPacked

The issues encountered were:
- Bridge was originally mapped to /robot1/scan instead of /robot1/points/points
- Bridge argument used @ on both sides causing a loopback condition
- The actual gpu_lidar packed output is on /robot1/points/points, not
    /robot1/points as initially assumed

Nav2 costmap layers require sensor_msgs/LaserScan, not PointCloud2. The package ros-jazzy-velodyne-laserscan is installed and velodyne_laserscan_node is added
to the launch file. It subscribes to /robot1/points/points and publishes a flattened 2D scan to /robot1/scan by extracting a single horizontal ring from
the point cloud.

 /robot1/points/points  - sensor_msgs/PointCloud2
                           Published by: ros_gz_bridge
                           Consumed by:  velodyne_laserscan_node, RViz, SLAM

  /robot1/scan           - sensor_msgs/LaserScan
                           Published by: velodyne_laserscan_node
                           Consumed by:  Nav2 local_costmap
Both topics verified publishing at approximately 7Hz.

 - go2_description/xacro/velodyne.xacro exists in the repo but is not used.
    It depends on libgazebo_ros_velodyne_laser.so which is a classic Gazebo
    plugin incompatible with Gazebo Harmonic. All LiDAR functionality is handled
    through the gpu_lidar sensor in gazebo.xacro and the ros_gz_bridge.

